    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against higher xERA opponents. **Kyle Tucker** (72.53) leads the charge, providing the day\u2019s highest efficiency score; he benefits immensely from an excellent SP skill matchup and should thrive against the opposing lefty, provided he capitalizes on his order position. Not far behind, **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) are our strongest plays, both receiving significant boosts from park factors and weak opposing arms. **Heliot Ramos** in particular is positioned perfectly at the top of the lineup to capitalize on the 6.43 xERA of his matchup, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring potential.\n\nThe decision to bench **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46) was the most difficult call of the morning. While his raw hitting talent remains elite, the combination of a tough outing against Logan Gilbert and unfavorable park and platoon dynamics pushed his efficiency score below that of **Josh Lowe** (59.90) and **Andy Pages** (69.99). **Andy Pages** remains a high-upside play, with his speed-related situational bonus\u2014stemming from a slow opposing delivery\u2014keeping his score near the 70 threshold. We are monitoring the situation with **Jackson Merrill** closely; his status is officially \"Lineup Pending,\" and the assumption of a lower-order slot coupled with the elite pitching of Yamamoto creates a volatility floor that we must watch throughout the afternoon. While **Liam Hicks** (59.92) is active, ensure the lineup remains stable to protect our game caps against Civale\u2019s vulnerability.",
